    "body": "## Problem\n\n`2\"_x` deletes 4 chars instead of 2 (fixes #42468). Same for X, D, C, s, S and any register. Since 2514256d95, nv_optrans() runs the stuffed `2dl` right away through exec_stuffed(), while the count typed before `\"` is still in `opcount`. The nested normal_cmd() then multiplies it in a second time.\n\n## Solution\n\nClear `opcount` before running the stuffed keys, since they already contain the count. Added a functional test for x/X/D/s/S with a count before the register. It fails on master and passes with this change. I also ran mode_normal_spec, cmdatom_spec, count_spec and macro_spec locally.\n\nAI-assisted: the code and test were written mainly by an AI agent on my behalf.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
